  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>&nbsp;The alcohol is reacted with a mixture of sodium&nbsp;iodide and concentrated phosphoric&nbsp;acid, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi>PO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>, and the iodoalkane is distilled off. The 2-iodobutane formed in the previous reaction give Grignard reagent with magnesium metal in dry ether. The Grignard reagent formed reacts with&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></math>&nbsp;to give 2-deuterobutane.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e67d046b-9bff-4356-9e03-2b9f02b6ad59.png\" style=\"width: 544px; height: 203px;\" /></p>",
